            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nGigantic new indoor playground that's well- designed, above average quality and pricing\nJan 2021 • Family\nLocated within the newly built Saigon South Marina Club, this indoor playground is probably one of the largest in the area, occupying a fully glassed three-storey space on the club's higher floor. It has half floors within.\n\nThe huge space allows for a three-floor-high slide, sponge (not ball) pit, trampolines, both large and mini climbing structures, and for those who prefer a less active play: \n- drawing and 3D projections\n- fishing (with well-designed handles on fishing ropes and badge prizes to be won for 50 fishes caught!)\n- arrrow/dart-shooting\n- craft-making (but it probably depends on whether there are staff available to do so? We didn't see any class going on the few hours we were there).\n- probably other areas too which I'm not aware of. Less playthings for the really little ones. I guess they don't focus on toys but more on active play.\n\nSome areas I feel can be improved:\n- it is really hard to locate my children, especially during peak period when there seems to be hundreds of kids running around (one school excursion can bring >50 kids). Perhaps build in some camera/monitors?\n- the food is average at best, but prices are above average. Perhaps work on the food? My usd$8 corndog was obviously just heated up corndogs with a mini salad that's not very fresh.\n- we managed to get the promotional deal by getting 30 kids to visit, and the promotion states that each kid will get a free drink. It turned out to be plain water, and we weren't even served that at all.\n- there were no signages on the ground floor of the club, which looked like it was still under construction. Hard to find the way in without asking the security guard. We had to use a back door to enter the club.\n\nOverall, good concept, well-designed safety guards and play areas, mostly attentive staff, but still can be improved. Also, we spent over a hundred dollars for few hours of play there. Steep prices!\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 26, 2021\nKiwooza Planet\nHello Maryyeo, Thank you for your kind comment and your interest in our Kiwooza Planet. We are sorry for any inconvenience you had during your visit. From this April we are having our Korean Chef as he cannot be available during the pandemic. We promise to improve our fnb quality with our Korean brand standard. Moreover, we are providing more free board games and free massage therapy for parents while kids are playing. I hope you will find our place as your family favorite destination and continue to support us to growth\nRead more\nWritten April 14, 2021\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
